# Response headers for https://kcoap.dev (Workers Static Assets read this file; it is not served).
# web/README.md explains each header and links the Cloudflare documentation.
#
# Content-Security-Policy: the pages load only their own CSS, JavaScript and images, have no inline code
# (scripts/check-site fails on any), and make one request elsewhere: /releases/ asks the GitHub API for the
# latest releases. One policy covers every page, because Cloudflare joins two values of one header with a
# comma, and a browser then enforces both policies at once.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; connect-src https://api.github.com; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains

# Caching. Everything keeps Cloudflare's default, "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", with an ETag, unless
# a rule below says otherwise: the pages, the stylesheets and the scripts keep their names between deploys
# (they are not fingerprinted), so they revalidate on every load and always match. The images change
# rarely and may be kept a day. Each image has a rule of its own: Cloudflare documents a splat only at the
# end of a path, and no file may match two rules that set the same header (scripts/check-site checks both).

/assets/kcoap-logo.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/assets/og-image.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
